WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.480
Mr. Roswaal, is it true that we're
having a school festival soon?

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.310
A school festival?

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.150
It looks like it's true.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:09.230
"Rabbits"
"What do they eat?"

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.070
Nobody told us.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.570
Oh, I didn't teeeell you?

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.410
No.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.160
So, when is it?

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.870
Next week.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.450
That's really soon!

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.540
So, do we have to do something?

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.750
Correeeect!

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.510
And if you can make it a successsssss...

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.010
We might possibly, perchance,
mayhap, be able to go home.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:35.970
Nope!

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:06.930
"Episode 10: Rise Up! School Festival"

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:13.940
I believe that you'll make the
school festival a big successssss!

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.650
It sounds like fun!

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.450
A lot more fun than field day, anyway!

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.320
We can eat a lot of
yummy food at the stalls, too.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.990
Chocolate banana!

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.710
So, sir, what will be doing
at the festival as a class?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:33.460
Well, you have two things you'll be doing...

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.500
One, a food stall!

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.300
<i>Chocolate banana</i>!

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.140
And the other is a play!

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.260
A play!

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.980
Class 1 is doing <i>The Ugly
Duckling</i>, they saaaay.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.480
Sister, I don't need to turn around
to tell that you're looking at me.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.570
I'm not sitting here
thinking that you're ugly.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.690
I do find you disgusting, however.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.530
I saw that coming.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:03.370
You can see that far into the future?

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.990
While we're on the subject,

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:08.290
why don't we decide what
we'll be selling at our food stall,

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.620
and what we'll be doing in our plaaaaaaay!

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.370
"Nurse's Office"

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:16.960
So Class 2 ended up picking <i>Cinderella</i>, huh?

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.050
Indeed. It was a safe choice.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.890
It's a great story, though!

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.350
Right, Naofumi?

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.260
Yeah.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.680
I love the scene at the end where
the evil women get what's coming to them!

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.770
So you're the prince, Rem?

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.150
Yes. I'm the prince.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.320
And my sister is Cinderella.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:44.320
I'm very nervous about being her co-star,
but I'm going to do my best.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.200
You drew lots for it, huh?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.490
Yes. It's an amazing coincidence.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.290
I refuse to accept this.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:57.000
The only royalty in this world,
of any type, is Lord Ains!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.630
But if Ains is the prince,

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:04.090
that means he'll end up
with Ram, the princess.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.720
That can't happen!

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.260
Then it all worked out for the best, huh?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.930
But I can't accept the role he got!

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:15.060
What role did he get?

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.690
Lord Ains is with those humans...

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.480
Humans?

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.650
They're the horses.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:23.860
Horses?

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.160
He and the humans he worked with
during the field day

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.620
are going to be horses
that pull the carriage!

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.910
A Supreme Being, playing a horse?

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.250
What's wrong with being a horse?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.460
Everything!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:41.090
He's lucky. I'm The Ugly Duckling.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.590
--Sounds about right!
--Shalltear!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:48.470
Should I go watch you quack?

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:54.270
Maybe I'll go see your
Supreme Being neigh, then?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.060
Stop it, guys!

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:56.980
"7 Days Left"

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.690
What kind of scene can star a horse?

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.360
Let's do it!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:02.780
"6 Days Left"

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.530
You're good with that hammer.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.280
What about me?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.280
You're good with those fans.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.280
"5 Days Left"

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.620
Can you go out with me to get supplies?

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.830
Yes. Also, he means that he
wants me to go buy supplies with him,

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.460
not that he wants me to be his girlfriend.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.420
I know that! I know that!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.420
"4 Days Left"

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.380
Very well!

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.680
I, the beautiful and omnipotent goddess,
shall take you to the ball...

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.550
--Too long.
--Too long.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:30.350
It's my big scene, though!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.350
"3 Days Left"

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.520
Do we need this much chocolate?

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.430
We always need more chocolate!

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.730
That's right!

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.600
These two are a pain.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.610
"2 Days Left"

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.520
How could you be so cruel, sister?

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:46.950
Wait, am I bullying here?
Or am I being bullied?

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.740
Is this in the script?

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:49.740
"1 Day Left"

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.240
"School Festival"

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.830
We made it.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.500
Now we just need to make the
school festival a big success tomorrow.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.330
Yes.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:01.340
Let's go do the last rehearsal in the gym.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.250
Yeah!

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.840
Yeah!

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.590
Yeah!

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.260
Oh?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.850
What is this?

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.810
Just what it looks like.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.400
What about the demon beast inside?

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:28.780
That was no fun!

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.990
You're Hamsuke.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.160
That was close!

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.660
What happened here?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.290
Well you see,

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:48.260
Death Knight and I were taking a nap
in the sunlight when we heard a big noise!

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:52.220
Wh-What?

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:55.470
The next thing we knew, we were buried alive.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:58.850
This is expected, I wonder.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.730
What does that mean?

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.900
Everything that happens in this world

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:04.690
--Oh, Death Knight's back!
--is part of some grand design--

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.320
--Oh, Death Knight's back!
--Don't interrupt me!

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.780
What is this?

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.740
It's a mess.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.910
This is awful. What is this?

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:16.740
No idea...

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.000
Hey, what's wrong, everyone?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.460
Are you in awe of our grand creation?

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.590
We spent hours on that arch!

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:29.470
Looks like something big crushed it.

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:31.260
Is it somebody's idea of a prank?

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.430
That's not a fun prank.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.760
What's wrong with you?

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.470
What do you have against Mr. Archie?

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.980
Do you know how long I spent making him?

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:44.980
No, I'm the one who worked hard making him.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.570
Hey, don't cry.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.370
Aren't you glad you saw it on
the day before instead of tomorrow?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.450
Yeah. There's still time to remake it...

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:03.040
No! I don't want to remake him!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.250
--It was really hard!
--Aqua!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.050
No! No way!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.300
If you want to make it,
make it yourself, Kazuma!

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.470
Hell no!

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:15.220
We won't get it done by tomorrow
unless we all work together!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.470
Aqua.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.930
I said no, and when I said no, I meant no!

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.730
Aqua.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:33.360
Aqua, we need to make
the school festival a success.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.280
You understand that, right?

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.910
You don't need to tell me! I know!

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.540
That's why I worked hard!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.710
But look what happened to it!

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.790
We can't get it done by tomorrow!

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.040
Let's do our best.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.840
It's really hard!

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:50.130
Let's do our best.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.210
The pressure is incredible.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:56.760
If we have to get it done by tomorrow,
let's start it today!

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.260
Let's at least eat lunch first.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.600
Let's start now.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.440
There's no time,
so let's just do a half-assed job.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.560
--That's the best way--
--Let's do it right.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.610
From step one?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.400
No.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:13.820
From step zero!

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.620
What's going on?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.710
A really nice scene just got ruined.
That's what happened.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:54.040
Fine!

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.380
Is this your doing as well?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.920
Of course not.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:03.010
It's a sign that something beyond
our expectations is happpppening.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:08.390
And yet, the school festival must go on?

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:11.650
That won't change, I'm sure.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:15.980
Continuing this school life,

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.030
--and continuing to test them?

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.700
--Okay, let's get to work!
--and continuing to test them?

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.320
--Yeah, let's get to it!
--and continuing to test them?

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.610
--Yeah, let's get to it!
--That's the top priority

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.080
we've been given, huh?

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.790
As always, it's a tough job.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:32.790
The Goddess of Fate must have it out for us.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.420
There are no gods.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.090
Whether they exist or not,

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.090
--Emilia, hold that end, would you?
--who knows if the choice we're making

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.220
--Okay, got it.
--is the right one?

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:43.930
--Aqua, get to work!
--is the right one?

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:44.850
--Aqua, get to work!
--The answer is up to them, I supppppose.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.180
--It's heavy.
--The answer is up to them, I supppppose.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.640
--Let's do our best.
--The answer is up to them, I supppppose.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:52.190
--The answer is up to them, I supppppose.
